{{apichanges|10.2.0|prev=10.1.7|next=10.2.5}}

==Summary==
* Added a new [[#Texture_Slicing|texture slicing]] system that can be used as a replacement for backdrops and nineslice layouts.
* Addon management functions such as {{api|EnableAddOn}} and {{api|IsAddOnLoaded}} have been moved to the C_AddOns namespace.
** Most functions have the same signatures as before, however one exception to this is {{api|GetAddOnEnableState}} which had the order of its parameters swapped.
** Aliases from the old function names exist, but are deprecated and will be removed in a future patch.
* The {{api|GetCVarInfo}} function has been moved to the C_CVar namespace. An alias for the old name still exists, but is deprecated and will be removed in a future patch.
* The {{api|SetPortraitToTexture}} function now requires that the initial <code>texture</code> parameter be a texture object. Previously, this function would also accept string values if they named a global texture object.
* The C_Console namespace has been removed, with its functions moved back to the global namespace.
* The auto-generated API documentation has been expanded to include many global functions that were previously undocumented.
* The auto-generated API documentation [https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/349f1ecc1f4bec4dc7aae83985d6ebe8a7f2763a/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_APIDocumentationGenerated/PonyDocumentation.lua now contains a pony].
* Addons can no longer be loaded before FrameXML has fully loaded.
* Fixed an issue where newly created characters would have all addons enabled by default<ref>WoWUIBugs#41 https://github.com/Stanzilla/WoWUIBugs/issues/41</ref>.
* Fixed an issue where NaN values could be used as table keys.
* '''(Nov 16 2023)''' The {{api|CheckInteractDistance}} and {{api|IsItemInRange}} APIs are now protected and cannot be called by insecure code in combat as of build 52188.

